---
/** The club's signature.
 *
 *  Set in the site's own face rather than drawn. The mark it replaces was a
 *  bitmap wordmark — square, pixel-stepped letterforms — which put a second
 *  typographic culture on a page whose own wordmark is a grotesque. Two of
 *  those on one screen is what read as a toy.
 *
 *  Letterspaced and small, the way a signature at the foot of a page is set:
 *  it names who made this without competing with anything on it.
 */
---

<span class="club-mark">Vibe Coding Club</span>

<style>
	.club-mark {
		display: block;
		font-size: var(--size-club-mark, 0.875rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		/* Just enough to keep capitals from closing up at this size. Wider than
		   this and the words stop being words — the eye reads the gaps instead of
		   the line. */
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		/* The trailing letter's own spacing would push the line off centre. */
		text-indent: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		line-height: 1;
		white-space: nowrap;
		color: inherit;
	}
</style>
